+/* V3D has no dual source blending.  A D3D11 (DXVK) shader using it writes
+ * a second colour output (FRAG_RESULT_DATA0, index 1), which the backend would
+ * treat as a second variable for the same output and mix up with the first.
+ *
+ * exact_dual_src (the blend is ONE / ONE_MINUS_SRC1_ALPHA, see above): do the
+ * blend in the shader, out = out0 + dst * (1 - out1.a), with dst read from the
+ * tile buffer, and drop the second output; the hardware blend of that render
+ * target is disabled (v3dvx_pipeline.c). Folding instead (below) overwrote out0's
+ * own alpha with the coverage, which turned transparent shadow-layer fills
+ * (Edge canvas shadowBlur) into opaque black boxes.
+ *
+ * Otherwise: fold it into the alpha of output 0 (alpha = average of out1.rgb) and
+ * drop the second output.  Together with mapping the SRC1_* blend factors to
+ * SRC_ALPHA (v3dvx_pipeline.c) this reproduces grayscale ClearType. */
